  "semantic_notes": [
    {
      "heading": "[ edit 5 1 Quick Notes ]",
      "text": "An interlaced pentagram, this is known variously as the \"Cinquefoil Knot\", after certain herbs and shrubs of the rose family which have 5-lobed leaves and 5-petaled flowers (see e.g. [4] ), as the \"Pentafoil Knot\" (visit Bert Jagers' pentafoil page ), as the \"Double Overhand Knot\", as 5_1 , or finally as the torus knot T(5,2) . When taken off the post the strangle knot (hitch) of practical knot tying deforms to 5_1 [ edit 5 1 Further Notes and Views ] A kolam of a 2x3 dot array The VISA Interlink Logo [1] Version of the US bicentennial emblem A pentagonal table by Bob Mackay [2] The Utah State Parks logo As impossible object (\"Penrose\" pentagram)",
      "source": "rendered-text-window"
    },
    {
      "heading": "[ edit 5 1 Further Notes and Views ]",
      "text": "A kolam of a 2x3 dot array The VISA Interlink Logo [1] Version of the US bicentennial emblem A pentagonal table by Bob Mackay [2] The Utah State Parks logo As impossible object (\"Penrose\" pentagram) Folded ribbon which is single-sided (more complex version of Möbius Strip). Non-pentagonal shape. Pentagram of circles. Alternate pentagram of intersecting circles. 3D-looking rendition.",
      "source": "rendered-text-window"
    },
    {
      "heading": "[ edit Notes on presentations of 5 1 ]",
      "text": "Knot 5_1. A graph, knot 5_1.",
      "source": "rendered-text-window"
    }
  ],
